{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the guard detector/behavioral test to cover `monkeypatch.delattr` on a State (don't whitelist it), or prove delattr-on-State restores correctly.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_app_state_patch_guard.py:49 restricts the call check to `node.func.attr == \"setattr\"`","tests/unit/test_app_state_patch_guard.py:99 lists `'monkeypatch.delattr(appmod.app.state, \"queue\", raising=False)'` under `test_the_scan_allows_safe_forms`","test_review_bot_in_flight.py:145 and :183: `monkeypatch.delattr(appmod.app.state, \"queue\", raising=False)` — a delattr on a State, the same private `_state`-backed object the guard exists to protect","test_the_sanctioned_form_restores_a_present_entry_and_removes_an_absent_one only exercises `mp.setitem` (lines 116-117); no behavioral assertion that `monkeypatch.delattr` on a State restores a present entry under the pytest 9.2.0 __dict__ old-value bug"],"finding":"The new guard's detector (`_violations`) only inspects `setattr` calls and bare app.state assignments; it never inspects `monkeypatch.delattr(app.state, ...)` and explicitly whitelists that form as 'safe', yet `delattr` on a Starlette `State` is the same backing-dict operation the fix targets. The behavioral restore test covers only `setitem`, so the `delattr`-on-State restore seam used at test_review_bot_in_flight.py:145 and :183 is untested.","id":"0","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/unit/test_app_state_patch_guard.py:99","norm_id":"n560be06fb2f4e642","priority":0.2121,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenar